      "id": 1,
      "text": "Vernon was founded in 1817 by Zadok Casey, who later served as Illinois State Senator and lieutenant governor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Vernon%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was named after George Washington’s Mount Vernon plantation, itself named for British naval hero Edward Vernon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Vernon%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "When the town was first settled, there was no road leading to it, forcing travelers to navigate high ground or swamp crossings.",
